# ── Roule Rodrigues — environment variables ─────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env.local for development. On Vercel: Settings → Environment Variables.
# Most integrations can ALSO be configured from Admin → Alerts & Email with no
# redeploy — admin-saved values take priority over these env vars.

# Supabase (required)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=sb_secret_...   # server-only; never expose to the client

# Admin (required)
ADMIN_PASSWORD=choose-a-long-unique-password
SESSION_SECRET=any-long-random-string      # rotating it logs out all sessions

# ── Email (M41: both providers can carry transactional mail) ────────────────
# Routing, limits, thresholds and the ticketing reserve are configured in
# Admin → Alerts & Email, NOT here. These variables only supply credentials.
# Usage, failures and quota are visible in that same admin panel.

# Brevo — the default provider (or set from Admin → Alerts & Email)
BREVO_API_KEY=xkeysib-...
BREVO_FROM=Roule Rodrigues <you@gmail.com> # must be a verified Brevo sender
# Two SEPARATE lists, deliberately. Booking something is not marketing consent:
# every booking flow joins the transactional list, and only an explicit opt-in
# (waitlist / saved list) joins the marketing one. Never point both at one list.
BREVO_TRANSACTIONAL_LIST_ID=4              # optional: lifecycle automations
BREVO_LIST_ID=3                            # optional: campaign audience only
# NOTE: Brevo's free 300/day is shared with the SMTP relay Supabase Auth uses
# for password resets, so part of that ceiling is spent by traffic the app
# cannot count. The dashboard shows Brevo usage as a floor, not a total.

# Resend — second provider. Free tier is 3,000/month AND 100/day, 1 domain.
# BOTH are required for Resend to be usable: without RESEND_FROM the provider
# reports itself unconfigured and the router simply routes elsewhere. It does
# NOT fall back to onboarding@resend.dev, which can only deliver to your own
# Resend account address — that fallback silently broke every customer email.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# RESEND_FROM=Roule Rodrigues <bookings@yourdomain.com>  # verified domain

# Owner notifications
OWNER_EMAIL=you@gmail.com                  # receives booking alerts
OWNER_WHATSAPP=23058355588                 # used in email WhatsApp buttons
# CallMeBot WhatsApp alerts (or set from Admin → Alerts & Email)
CALLMEBOT_PHONE=23058355588
CALLMEBOT_APIKEY=1234567

# Cron (required in production — the daily reminder job FAILS CLOSED without it)
CRON_SECRET=any-long-random-string

# Shared rate limiting — Upstash Redis (strongly recommended in production).
# Without these, rate limits are in-memory PER SERVERLESS INSTANCE, so the real
# ceiling is limit × instances. With them, every instance shares one counter.
# Free tier is enough. Create a database at console.upstash.com → REST API tab.
# Absent = the in-memory limiter stays in charge; nothing breaks either way.
# Check which mode is live at /api/health → checks.rateLimiter.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://YOUR-DB.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=...

# PostHog (optional product analytics)
#
# CANONICAL NAME: NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY — that is what the PostHog UI calls it
# ("project API key") and what the Vercel project already uses. Set that one.
#
# The code reads NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY first and falls back to
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN. The fallback is not decoration: a platform
# variable outranks .env.production even when it is BLANK, so if Vercel's
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY were ever emptied it would shadow the committed value
# and take analytics down. .env.production therefore keeps the token under the
# legacy name, where a blank platform var cannot shadow it. Do not "tidy" the
# two names into one without re-reading instrumentation-client.ts.
#
# The token is public by design (NEXT_PUBLIC_*, shipped to every browser); it is
# not a secret and committing it is intentional. Absent = analytics off and
# nothing breaks — the site still runs, it just records nothing.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_your_project_token
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com

# PostHog silence alarm (optional, server-side). Without this the daily
# /api/cron/posthog-health check runs and reports "not_configured" instead of
# verifying that real events are still arriving. This one IS a secret — create a
# Personal API Key in PostHog with project "Query" read scope.
# POSTHOG_PERSONAL_API_KEY=phx_...
# POSTHOG_PROJECT_ID=244679                 # defaults to the live project
# POSTHOG_API_HOST=https://eu.posthog.com   # app host, not the ingestion host

# Optional
GOOGLE_REVIEW_URL=https://g.page/r/...     # feedback emails link here
HOLD_EXPIRY_HOURS=48                       # pending bookings auto-release after this
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=fc-...                    # web scraping/research CLI (dev tooling only)

# ── SHARPER SATELLITE IMAGERY (optional, all three or none) ─────────────────
#
# The shipped satellite layer is EOX's hosted Sentinel-2 cloudless: 2016, and
# 10 m/pixel, so it goes soft above zoom 14. Two things are wrong with it —
# it looks dated, and EOX's HOSTED tiles are CC BY-NC-SA. Non-commercial. This
# is a commercial marketplace. The Copernicus data underneath is free for
# commercial use; it is EOX's hosting of it that is not.
#
# lib/tracking/tiles.ts reads these three and needs no code change. It takes
# all three or none: a custom layer carrying EOX's attribution credits the
# wrong people, and one with no attribution breaks the licence of every
# provider there is, so a half-filled swap falls back rather than shipping
# something unlawful.
#
# Mapbox Satellite is the recommended source — sub-metre over Rodrigues, 750k
# tile requests a month free, commercial use permitted. Mapbox does require a
# card on file to create the account. Restrict the token to roulerodrig.com in
# the Mapbox dashboard before using it: NEXT_PUBLIC_ means it ships to every
# browser, and the URL restriction is what stops somebody else spending your
# free tier.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_SATELLITE_URL=https://api.mapbox.com/v4/mapbox.satellite/{z}/{x}/{y}@2x.jpg90?access_token=pk.your_token
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_SATELLITE_ATTRIBUTION=&copy; <a href="https://www.mapbox.com/about/maps/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mapbox</a> &copy; <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap</a>
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_SATELLITE_MAX_NATIVE_ZOOM=18
